<<~ ahu slot=`#/witness-pattern-to-prevent-regrowth`>>

!! Witness pattern to prevent regrowth

Guard ''current writer/reader shape agreement'', rather than a list of retired literals. A witness can enumerate each house-owned persisted format and assert that current writers emit one grammar, readers do not accept a second house grammar, and upgrade callbacks contain no deletion of house-owned old stores. It should also flag history-named refusal kinds and exception-list entries that exist solely to allow an earlier spelling; review each hit against live hostile-input guards. The two clearest seeds are the digest writer/parser mismatch (`packages/lararium-tw5/src/memetic-wikitext-sensorium.ts:169`, `packages/lararium-mesh/src/agile-digest.ts:127`) and IDB deletes (`packages/lararium-browser/src/browser-vessel-identity.ts:99`).

